WEBVTT

00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:03.430
<i>Anime Ja Nai
It's not Anime!</i>

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:06.520
<i>Anime Ja Nai
It's not Anime</i>

00:00:08.310 --> 00:00:11.320
<i>Hontou no koto sa
It really is real!</i>

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.280
<i>GUNDAM</i>

00:00:12.690 --> 00:00:16.280
<i>MOBILE SUIT</i>

00:00:13.200 --> 00:00:16.280
<i>Minna ga neshizumatta yoru
In the night when everyone else was lost in their sleep...</i>

00:00:16.280 --> 00:00:18.620
<i>Mado kara sora wo miru to
I looked at the sky through the window...</i>

00:00:18.620 --> 00:00:23.540
<i>Tottemo sugoi mono wo mita n' da
...and there I saw such a great thing!</i>

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.840
<i>Otona wa dare mo warai-nagara
All the adults told me with a great big laugh...</i>

00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:31.340
<i>Terebi no misugi to iu kedo
"You've been watching way too much television again!"</i>

00:00:31.340 --> 00:00:34.920
<i>Boku wa zettai ni zettai ni
But I would never, ever...</i>

00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:37.140
<i>Uso nanka itte 'nai
...tell any kind of lie!</i>

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:45.520
<i>Joushiki to iu megane de
This world of ours...</i>

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:51.020
<i>Boku-tachi no sekai wa
...cannot be viewed through...</i>

00:00:51.940 --> 00:00:54.820
<i>Nozokeya shinai no sa
...the glasses of common sense.</i>

00:00:54.820 --> 00:00:58.320
<i>Yume wo wasureta
You old earthlings...</i>

00:00:58.320 --> 00:01:02.830
<i>furui chikyuu-jin yo
...who have forgotten your dreams!</i>

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.830
<i>Anime Ja Nai! Anime Ja Nai!
It's not Anime! It's not Anime!</i>

00:01:07.830 --> 00:01:10.330
<i>Fushigi na kimochi
Such a wonderful feeling!</i>

00:01:11.040 --> 00:01:12.420
<i>Anime Ja Nai
It's not Anime!</i>

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:15.840
<i>Anime Ja Nai
It's not Anime!</i>

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:20.140
<i>Hontou no koto sa
It really is real!</i>

00:01:22.010 --> 00:01:25.020
<i>Hontou no koto sa
It really is real!</i>

00:01:33.750 --> 00:01:36.920
We can laugh about it
now that it's all over,

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:39.800
but Gemon and that
Yazan guy showed up again.

00:01:39.800 --> 00:01:44.760
We were so desperate to get the Argama
out of the colony we got our wires crossed.

00:01:44.970 --> 00:01:48.100
We allowed the two of them
to come dangerously close to the Argama...

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.310
while the Zeta wasn't
working that well.

00:01:50.310 --> 00:01:53.430
I ended up having
to use my rifle on them.

00:01:55.890 --> 00:02:00.020
JUDAU IN SPACE

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:10.910
This is our colony, Shangri-La,
seen from the outside.

00:02:12.160 --> 00:02:14.710
This is the
spaceport gate.

00:02:16.750 --> 00:02:22.460
And this is Mashymre, Mr. Rose Guy,
launching the Endra out of Shangri-La.

00:02:22.460 --> 00:02:25.760
Dedication like his is
a real headache for us.

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.080
Great...

00:02:57.790 --> 00:03:00.670
La Vie en Rose,
where are you?

00:03:01.960 --> 00:03:05.460
Core Fighter, aren't we at the
La Vie en Rose rendezvous point yet?

00:03:05.460 --> 00:03:10.470
I'll find it soon!
Blame it on all this debris.

00:03:15.850 --> 00:03:19.810
- She says it'll be soon.
- She's been saying that for a while now!

00:03:20.770 --> 00:03:23.360
Hey! Have you spotted
anything nearby?

00:03:23.360 --> 00:03:24.270
Hey!

00:03:24.270 --> 00:03:26.650
Let's see... Two plus two is...

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:31.740
Hey!

00:03:32.160 --> 00:03:33.280
You're on watch!

00:03:33.280 --> 00:03:36.080
Um, yes, sir!
Nothing unusual, sir!

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:38.960
Same here!
Nothing but debris, sir!

00:03:38.960 --> 00:03:40.580
Can't you be serious?!

00:03:40.580 --> 00:03:42.250
Sorry, sir!

00:03:42.250 --> 00:03:45.380
His attitude's totally changed
since we left Shangri-La!

00:03:45.380 --> 00:03:46.960
What's his problem?

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:50.050
Shinta! Give it back!

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:50.880
No!

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:52.680
This isn't a playground!

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.390
I brought this for
you to see, Captain!

00:03:56.180 --> 00:03:59.850
It's too big. It has to be
smaller, or we can't use it.

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:00.980
I got it!

00:04:00.980 --> 00:04:03.480
Qum! That's not a toy!

00:04:03.480 --> 00:04:06.360
- You can't have it!
- Give it back!

00:04:06.980 --> 00:04:09.780
My god... What's happened
to my ship?

00:04:09.780 --> 00:04:11.570
That girl's lost, sir.

00:04:11.570 --> 00:04:14.160
So why doesn't
she say that herself?!

00:04:14.160 --> 00:04:17.160
She seems like the stubborn type.
She'll never say so.

00:04:17.160 --> 00:04:18.580
We'll search for it, as well!

00:04:18.580 --> 00:04:20.790
She'll be mad if we find it first.

00:04:20.790 --> 00:04:22.960
We can't humor her childishness!

00:04:22.960 --> 00:04:24.580
I suppose so, but...

00:04:24.580 --> 00:04:26.380
Keithron, you're on radar!

00:04:26.380 --> 00:04:27.880
Aye, sir.

00:04:27.880 --> 00:04:31.090
Minovsky particle density shouldn't
be that high, so limit the direction...

00:04:31.090 --> 00:04:33.590
of your sweeps to avoid
detection by enemy ships.

00:04:33.590 --> 00:04:34.640
Aye, sir!

00:04:41.640 --> 00:04:43.980
- Mr. Tragier?
- Yeah?

00:04:43.980 --> 00:04:46.060
You're not repairing the Methuss?

00:04:46.060 --> 00:04:49.280
I can't spare the manpower.
It'll fly if you need it to.

00:04:49.360 --> 00:04:50.650
Fa!

00:04:51.030 --> 00:04:53.990
We've finished a lot
of dummy asteroids!

00:04:53.990 --> 00:04:55.950
That's dangerous!
Get off that!

00:04:56.780 --> 00:04:58.870
Okay, here we go!

00:05:00.790 --> 00:05:02.660
This is the seed for
a dummy asteroid?

00:05:02.660 --> 00:05:04.080
Kinda small, isn't it?

00:05:04.080 --> 00:05:06.080
Here! Ready, set...

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:08.960
Wow! That's great!

00:05:08.960 --> 00:05:12.510
They can expand to 50 times
their original size out in space.

00:05:12.550 --> 00:05:13.760
That much?

00:05:13.760 --> 00:05:17.050
You could hide a mobile suit
in something that size, easily!

00:05:17.050 --> 00:05:18.260
Exactly!

00:05:18.260 --> 00:05:20.680
The dummies don't have to
just look like asteroids, either.

00:05:20.680 --> 00:05:22.060
Right!

00:05:23.480 --> 00:05:24.270
What's this?

00:05:24.270 --> 00:05:27.020
A dummy made to look like
colony wreckage. Now watch.

00:05:34.360 --> 00:05:35.490
Cool!

00:05:35.490 --> 00:05:37.160
It was so little.

00:05:37.990 --> 00:05:40.950
With enough of them,
we can hide the Argama.

00:05:40.950 --> 00:05:43.660
And if you attach bombs to them,
they become mines.

00:05:43.660 --> 00:05:44.960
That's right.

00:05:44.960 --> 00:05:47.670
Easier to use than
Minovsky particles, huh?

00:05:47.670 --> 00:05:50.460
We can use them in
mobile suit battles, too.

00:05:50.460 --> 00:05:55.220
So why didn't you use dummy asteroids
 when you were piloting the Methuss, Mr. Torres?

00:05:56.260 --> 00:05:58.090
You just pounded the other guy.

00:05:58.140 --> 00:06:01.680
Because he was inside the colony.
Right, Torres?

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:03.520
Yeah!
Um, right! That's why!

00:06:07.060 --> 00:06:10.570
Gather around, everyone!
Have a look at the room assignments!

00:06:10.570 --> 00:06:12.070
What? Room assignments?

00:06:12.070 --> 00:06:13.360
Don't just pick them!

00:06:13.360 --> 00:06:17.490
It's fine! If we'd asked everybody,
we'd never have been able to decide.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:19.160
Will we have to change, as well?

00:06:19.160 --> 00:06:22.160
I figured this would work better
in case of emergencies.

00:06:23.410 --> 00:06:24.790
It's like being in school!

00:06:24.790 --> 00:06:26.460
Iino, come on!

00:06:26.460 --> 00:06:27.250
Where?

00:06:27.250 --> 00:06:29.080
Just shut up and come!

00:06:35.380 --> 00:06:37.880
Hurry! If we send out
a strong radio transmission,

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.760
the Endra will detect
the Argama's position!

00:06:40.760 --> 00:06:42.680
-I'm not doing this!
- Iino!

00:06:42.680 --> 00:06:45.140
Selling the Argama out
is just dirty!

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:46.980
Wait!

00:06:46.980 --> 00:06:51.270
Think about it. They're never
going to win at this rate!

00:06:51.270 --> 00:06:54.360
Better we sell the Argama
to the Endra...

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.070
and go back to
Shangri-La, right?

00:06:56.070 --> 00:06:58.570
I don't want to betray the
people on the Argama!

00:06:58.570 --> 00:07:03.080
Listen! We've lived our lives without
relying on any adults, right?!

00:07:03.080 --> 00:07:05.080
That doesn't change out in space!

00:07:05.080 --> 00:07:09.460
You think Judau's gonna last long here?
You really think he's a Newtype?!

00:07:12.250 --> 00:07:16.090
So come on. Let's go back to
Shangri-La and be friends again.

00:07:16.090 --> 00:07:20.260
If we sell them the Argama,
we'll get money to buy a new mobile suit!

00:07:20.260 --> 00:07:23.890
- We'd be junk dealers again?!
- What's wrong with it?! Fine!

00:07:23.890 --> 00:07:24.890
Don't!

00:07:24.890 --> 00:07:26.470
- Outta the way!
- I said stop!

00:07:26.470 --> 00:07:29.440
Hey, you!
What are you doing in here?

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:32.560
- Well, we're not used to the Argama yet.
- We got lost!

00:07:32.560 --> 00:07:35.280
- You coming back to the mobile suit deck?
- Right!

00:07:35.650 --> 00:07:36.690
Miss Fa!

00:07:36.900 --> 00:07:38.860
What are you up to, Iino?

00:07:47.790 --> 00:07:49.870
You picked up a
powerful radio signal?

00:07:49.870 --> 00:07:53.960
Aye, sir. It only lasted a few seconds,
but it was unusually strong.

00:07:53.960 --> 00:07:55.170
The Argama.

00:07:55.170 --> 00:07:56.880
Did you confirm the location?

00:07:56.880 --> 00:07:59.470
But that isn't like the Argama.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.970
It was like they were
asking to be found.

00:08:01.970 --> 00:08:05.560
Fool! There must be a traitor
aboard the Argama.

00:08:05.560 --> 00:08:06.680
Huh?

00:08:06.680 --> 00:08:11.560
Our efforts to be friends with the
residents of Shangri-La have borne fruit!

00:08:11.560 --> 00:08:15.190
An Axis sympathizer is
aboard the Argama!

00:08:15.190 --> 00:08:17.070
Isn't it fantastic?

00:08:17.280 --> 00:08:19.780
Lady Haman, we've done it!

00:08:21.660 --> 00:08:23.950
Is that clear, Mashymre?

00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:28.580
It's a fine commander who
gains the trust of the citizens.

00:08:29.580 --> 00:08:33.750
To that end, you must show
them kindness and sympathy.

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:34.670
My lady!

00:08:34.670 --> 00:08:38.090
A leader needs to possess
such consideration.

00:08:38.090 --> 00:08:40.170
Do you understand, Mashymre?

00:08:40.170 --> 00:08:41.380
I do!

00:08:46.180 --> 00:08:49.770
I shall show that consideration
with all my heart, Lady Haman!

00:08:51.270 --> 00:08:53.850
Traitor? You mean a spy?

00:08:53.850 --> 00:08:57.570
We'll show them the sincerity of Axis!
I'll go out in the Hamma-Hamma!

00:08:57.570 --> 00:08:58.650
Master Mashymre!

00:08:58.650 --> 00:09:01.110
I'm sure Lady Haman would approve.

00:09:01.280 --> 00:09:01.990
Let's go!

00:09:01.990 --> 00:09:04.070
Wait! Master Mashymre!

00:09:04.070 --> 00:09:06.570
Please take some
Gaza-Cs as an escort!

00:09:06.570 --> 00:09:10.580
I said I didn't want them,
and I meant it! Behold, this mobile suit!

00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:14.960
The impressive look! The sheer mass!
The Zeta Gundam is nothing compared to this!

00:09:14.960 --> 00:09:19.250
The new Hamma-Hamma
is the ultimate mobile suit!

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:22.380
So long as I have this,
my victory is assured!

00:09:22.670 --> 00:09:25.390
We beg of you, Master Mashymre!

00:09:25.890 --> 00:09:27.010
Wh-What?!

00:09:27.010 --> 00:09:31.520
We ask that you allow us
to assist you, Master Mashymre!

00:09:32.680 --> 00:09:36.940
You guys... I see.
Do as you wish!

00:09:37.980 --> 00:09:40.650
I was given good men.

00:09:41.650 --> 00:09:43.530
Hamma-Hamma, moving out!

00:09:50.790 --> 00:09:52.410
Space... it's been so long.

00:09:52.410 --> 00:09:55.000
My heart is dancing.
Wait for me, Argama!

00:10:03.880 --> 00:10:08.390
Papa. Mama. At last,
I'll be in a real mobile suit battle!

00:10:08.390 --> 00:10:09.720
Please, watch me!

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:19.520
Why are they flying around like that?
They can't settle down, can they?

00:10:31.450 --> 00:10:33.330
Now I can't find the Argama!

00:10:34.080 --> 00:10:37.080
For crying out loud,
I told them to follow me!

00:10:37.710 --> 00:10:38.290
Found it!

00:10:41.540 --> 00:10:44.840
Or maybe not.
What is that?

00:10:51.260 --> 00:10:52.600
Yikes...

00:10:53.140 --> 00:10:54.770
Hm? A child?

00:10:54.770 --> 00:10:59.230
Hey, look up at me! What's your unit?
What's your rank and full name?

00:10:59.270 --> 00:11:02.190
R-Rank and full name?

00:11:02.190 --> 00:11:05.780
Um, I'm not exactly
clear on that myself.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:07.070
Why not?

00:11:07.070 --> 00:11:09.360
I got recruited
suddenly in Colony 15...

00:11:09.360 --> 00:11:11.990
and they sent me out in
this little plane for training.

00:11:12.080 --> 00:11:15.830
Then I got lost, and now
I have no idea where I am!

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:17.460
Hmm... you're lost?

00:11:17.460 --> 00:11:18.580
Yes!

00:11:18.580 --> 00:11:22.670
I don't know if she's AEUG or Federation,
but she's just a young girl.

00:11:24.750 --> 00:11:28.050
Glemy Toto, take this girl
to the Endra.

00:11:28.510 --> 00:11:33.680
What? Master Mashymre,
this is my first battle.

00:11:33.680 --> 00:11:37.480
A first battle's like a
birthday for us rookie pilots.

00:11:38.060 --> 00:11:41.270
All I ever get is back talk.
Can't you just shut up?

00:11:41.270 --> 00:11:43.270
Yes, sir! I will, but...

00:11:43.270 --> 00:11:44.360
Then do it!

00:11:44.360 --> 00:11:48.780
Jeez, why is Master Mashymre
such a sucker for women?

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:49.860
Glemy Toto!

00:11:49.860 --> 00:11:51.320
Um, yes, sir!

00:11:59.410 --> 00:12:01.670
Wow. She's cute.

00:12:13.180 --> 00:12:15.180
Um, please, everyone.

00:12:15.220 --> 00:12:18.890
I think I can get back on my own.
No need to worry about me.

00:12:18.980 --> 00:12:20.310
What are you saying?

00:12:20.310 --> 00:12:23.560
We of Axis are on
the side of citizens like you!

00:12:23.980 --> 00:12:26.690
Glemy Toto, don't let
anything happen to her.

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:27.860
Yes, sir!

00:12:33.660 --> 00:12:35.620
So this is the Earth Sphere.

00:12:35.620 --> 00:12:38.950
And there are girls here you
can fall in love with at first sight.

00:12:38.950 --> 00:12:40.870
Thank you, Lady Haman!

00:12:41.370 --> 00:12:44.580
Well, I dodged
that bullet, but now...

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:46.790
Oh well. Let's see
how this works out.

00:13:00.480 --> 00:13:01.770
Captain.

00:13:01.810 --> 00:13:02.390
What?

00:13:02.390 --> 00:13:04.600
Well, there's something
I'd like to tell you.

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:05.190
Hm?

00:13:05.190 --> 00:13:06.360
Enemy mobile suits!

00:13:06.360 --> 00:13:07.320
What?!

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:11.650
The ones from before! No!
There's a different one, too!

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:14.360
Level one battle stations!
Launch the Zeta Gundam!

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:16.870
Aye, sir! Mobile suits!

00:13:16.870 --> 00:13:18.660
Deploy dummy asteroids!

00:13:18.660 --> 00:13:20.950
Um, Captain Bright?

00:13:20.950 --> 00:13:24.210
Tell Judau to hurry!
We'll use the guns till he launches!

00:13:24.250 --> 00:13:25.170
Sir?

00:13:25.170 --> 00:13:26.460
Monitors, all!

00:13:26.460 --> 00:13:27.380
Aye, sir!

00:13:29.880 --> 00:13:32.470
Judau, I need to
tell you something!

00:13:32.470 --> 00:13:34.970
Get a normal suit on
before you get killed!

00:13:34.970 --> 00:13:36.390
What are you doing?!

00:13:36.390 --> 00:13:37.680
Judau!

00:13:41.850 --> 00:13:44.270
Bridge, do you have
a count on the enemies?

00:13:44.270 --> 00:13:45.350
We're not sure!

00:13:45.350 --> 00:13:47.110
Are you deploying any other mobile suits?

00:13:47.110 --> 00:13:47.980
We're not sure!

00:13:47.980 --> 00:13:49.110
What? Screw that!

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:52.490
You're in no position to argue!

00:13:52.490 --> 00:13:55.570
You've flown the Zeta longer than
anyone else in the Argama's crew!

00:13:56.070 --> 00:13:58.570
You're better than Fa!

00:13:58.570 --> 00:14:00.580
That's a harsh thing to say.

00:14:00.580 --> 00:14:03.910
Astonaige, kick the Zeta's ass!
Just get it launched!

00:14:03.960 --> 00:14:05.620
Be reasonable, sir!

00:14:05.750 --> 00:14:07.830
Flatter him!
Tell Judau he's a Newtype!

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:08.540
Aye, sir!

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:11.750
- Where are you going?
- I don't want to go!

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:14.670
Look, if the Argama goes
down, you die either way!

00:14:14.670 --> 00:14:17.220
Meaning what?
It's better I get killed first?!

00:14:17.680 --> 00:14:20.560
You won't get killed.
You're a Newtype.

00:14:20.560 --> 00:14:23.680
It's obvious from the way you've
been handling the Zeta so far!

00:14:23.680 --> 00:14:24.980
You're just flattering me.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:27.600
I'm not buying it!
I'm outta here!

00:14:27.650 --> 00:14:29.690
You've got nowhere to go!

00:14:29.690 --> 00:14:33.480
Don't you care if your friends
aboard from Shangri-La get killed?!

00:14:34.070 --> 00:14:35.400
Oh...!

00:14:35.820 --> 00:14:37.780
Your little sister's aboard, too!

00:14:37.820 --> 00:14:39.740
I know. I'm closing
the lid on this thing!

00:14:46.080 --> 00:14:48.790
We count 5 enemies!
Possibly more.

00:14:49.460 --> 00:14:51.960
What am I supposed
to say when I do this?

00:14:51.960 --> 00:14:52.960
Oh, yeah!

00:14:52.960 --> 00:14:55.300
Judau Ashta!
Zeta Gundam, here I go!

00:14:59.260 --> 00:15:02.140
Judau forgot to take an
energy pack for his rifle!

00:15:02.140 --> 00:15:03.140
What?!

00:15:06.560 --> 00:15:09.440
Come on, let's make some
food for the battle.

00:15:09.480 --> 00:15:11.190
Shinta, Qum,
can you help me?

00:15:11.190 --> 00:15:13.780
We just finished getting
ready for lunch, though.

00:15:13.780 --> 00:15:15.530
Don't the enemies eat lunch?

00:15:15.530 --> 00:15:17.490
Maybe they're fighting
on an empty stomach.

00:15:17.490 --> 00:15:19.490
Maybe that's why
they're always so weak.

00:15:19.490 --> 00:15:21.070
You're in the way!

00:15:21.070 --> 00:15:22.870
Man a gun turret somewhere!

00:15:22.870 --> 00:15:23.580
Y-Yes, sir!

00:15:29.670 --> 00:15:31.170
Oh, jeez...

00:15:33.250 --> 00:15:36.800
There's so much data,
I can't read it all! Let's see...

00:15:42.760 --> 00:15:45.850
I'm not a machine!
I can't do this all at once!

00:15:47.850 --> 00:15:51.600
What happened to Roux?
Did the enemies get her?

00:15:54.980 --> 00:15:55.860
What's that?!

00:15:58.280 --> 00:16:01.200
Excellent!
The Zeta Gundam came out alone.

00:16:03.410 --> 00:16:05.410
No fair!
There's only one of me!

00:16:09.960 --> 00:16:12.920
All right! All right!
No need to hold back out here in space!

00:16:16.960 --> 00:16:18.840
I'm out of energy!

00:16:20.680 --> 00:16:22.760
Crap!
I forgot my energy pack!

00:16:24.890 --> 00:16:26.180
Have at you, Zeta!

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:31.190
Bracing yourself
doesn't work in space!

00:16:35.690 --> 00:16:37.070
At this rate...!

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:39.360
Didn't you say fighting
isn't all about strength?

00:16:39.360 --> 00:16:41.200
That's right!
There are those dummy asteroids!

00:16:44.570 --> 00:16:45.910
He threw his beam rifle away?

00:16:49.080 --> 00:16:50.370
You flee?!

00:16:56.250 --> 00:16:59.090
The Zeta Gundam
doesn't have a beam rifle!

00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:02.510
All units, close range
and pursue! GO!

00:17:19.070 --> 00:17:21.650
They work hard, even in the
middle of a battle, huh?

00:17:21.650 --> 00:17:25.070
Miss Roux, there are no faults
in your plane's electrical systems.

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:27.990
Oh, really?
Should have known.

00:17:28.780 --> 00:17:30.370
What is this plane?

00:17:30.370 --> 00:17:34.290
It has good engines for something so small,
and it's got machine guns, too.

00:17:34.330 --> 00:17:35.710
Must be for show.

00:17:35.710 --> 00:17:37.460
They're real. They work.

00:17:37.460 --> 00:17:39.380
What?! This can shoot?!

00:17:39.380 --> 00:17:41.760
The AEUG might be officially
adopting this design.

00:17:43.760 --> 00:17:45.470
Miss Roux.

00:17:45.470 --> 00:17:48.390
If I stay here,
I'll get caught in the battle!

00:17:48.390 --> 00:17:50.810
Oh, Father and Mother
back in the colony!

00:17:50.810 --> 00:17:54.270
I'll never be naughty again!
I'll be a good girl!

00:17:54.270 --> 00:17:57.610
Roux Louka...
Do you want to go home?

00:17:57.940 --> 00:17:59.570
Yes!

00:18:03.990 --> 00:18:05.860
Will these dummy
asteroids hold out?

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:16.080
You can't escape us by
hiding among the asteroids, Zeta!

00:18:21.090 --> 00:18:24.420
Dummies? Now I'm getting irritated!
Come back here, Zeta!

00:18:27.090 --> 00:18:28.760
These balloons are in my way!

00:18:31.060 --> 00:18:34.060
Gaza-C team! Don't be fooled
by these dummy asteroids!

00:18:34.060 --> 00:18:35.560
Don't hesitate!
Charge!

00:18:35.560 --> 00:18:36.890
Oh, you stubborn...!

00:18:40.860 --> 00:18:43.360
You think you can use
those dummies forever?!

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:45.900
What?!

00:18:48.070 --> 00:18:50.870
Fools! They're just letting
themselves get hit?!

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:53.290
Can't they tell the real
ones from the fakes?!

00:18:54.950 --> 00:18:57.750
I don't believe this!
They're barely trained as pilots!

00:19:01.340 --> 00:19:05.090
I saw three flashes!
In that case...!

00:19:08.470 --> 00:19:11.890
Just one?
That doesn't match my count.

00:19:11.890 --> 00:19:13.060
Coward!

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:14.350
What did you say?!

00:19:14.350 --> 00:19:17.140
I said using dummy
asteroids is cowardly!

00:19:17.350 --> 00:19:19.810
And fighting five on one isn't?!

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:24.400
Well, we're one-on-one now!
You have no reason to complain!

00:19:24.440 --> 00:19:28.280
All's well that ends well?
I hate people who say that!

00:19:34.410 --> 00:19:35.700
What's...?

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:39.000
Miss Roux, it's an enemy
mobile suit! Be careful!

00:19:39.460 --> 00:19:41.960
What? That's the
Zeta Gundam, isn't it?

00:19:41.960 --> 00:19:43.750
All right! I'm in luck!

00:19:43.750 --> 00:19:44.460
Huh?

00:19:44.460 --> 00:19:46.380
Thanks for bringing
me out here!

00:19:49.510 --> 00:19:50.970
Miss Roux!

00:19:52.760 --> 00:19:53.470
Roux!

00:19:54.010 --> 00:19:55.390
Gaza-C...

00:19:55.390 --> 00:19:58.390
That fighter! It's the same one
we saw at Shangri-La, isn't it?!

00:20:00.270 --> 00:20:01.230
Why, that...!

00:20:06.730 --> 00:20:09.860
Miss Roux! Why'd you come
back after you attacked me?

00:20:09.860 --> 00:20:12.490
I'm sorry, Glemy.
You're not hurt, are you?

00:20:12.490 --> 00:20:16.080
N-No, but why did
you come back?

00:20:16.080 --> 00:20:18.700
Because I was worried
I might have hurt you.

00:20:19.580 --> 00:20:20.790
Worried?

00:20:20.790 --> 00:20:23.170
Because you were nice to me.

00:20:23.170 --> 00:20:26.550
I'm sorry, but I'm helping
out the Argama!

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:32.720
Roux Louka!
Master Mashymre?

00:20:35.260 --> 00:20:38.680
Miss Roux!
Master Mashymre is after you!

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:42.270
Uh-oh...

00:20:42.270 --> 00:20:44.610
I'm forgetting what I decided
to bear as my destiny.

00:20:45.110 --> 00:20:46.650
I won't forgive this!

00:20:48.530 --> 00:20:49.650
You're first?!

00:20:52.700 --> 00:20:54.320
Uh-oh!
He's way more powerful!

00:20:56.990 --> 00:20:58.120
I have you!

00:20:59.370 --> 00:21:00.330
What?!

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:01.960
Gotcha!

00:21:06.750 --> 00:21:08.670
If I were just wearing
a normal suit...!

00:21:11.550 --> 00:21:13.260
Running before
the fight's settled?!

00:21:15.050 --> 00:21:16.260
Say what you like!

00:21:16.260 --> 00:21:18.720
But we have a collaborator
aboard the Argama!

00:21:19.180 --> 00:21:22.980
Divine justice will eventually come
to one as cowardly as you!

00:21:32.360 --> 00:21:33.820
I don't get it!

00:21:33.820 --> 00:21:36.410
You sucker-punched that guy,
then ran without doing any more!

00:21:36.950 --> 00:21:39.870
Grown-ups have their reasons.

00:21:39.870 --> 00:21:42.290
You definitely could have
taken out one mobile suit!

00:21:42.580 --> 00:21:44.080
Listen, you!

00:21:44.080 --> 00:21:47.170
I was a girl being held
hostage aboard the Endra!

00:21:47.170 --> 00:21:50.840
You have no idea what I had
to suffer to get out of there!

00:21:51.170 --> 00:21:52.880
You didn't just get lost?

00:21:52.880 --> 00:21:55.470
Of course not!
I'm not that stupid!

00:21:55.470 --> 00:21:56.470
I couldn't tell!

00:21:56.470 --> 00:21:57.470
EXCUSE ME?!

00:21:57.470 --> 00:21:58.890
Stop it!

00:21:58.890 --> 00:22:01.680
Judau, you're sure the enemy
said there's a "collaborator" aboard?

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:03.060
Yeah.

00:22:03.060 --> 00:22:04.560
What did he mean?

00:22:04.560 --> 00:22:06.560
I think he was just
getting in a parting shot.

00:22:06.600 --> 00:22:08.900
I wouldn't worry
too much about it.

00:22:08.900 --> 00:22:10.440
How do you know?

00:22:10.440 --> 00:22:12.650
You sure you didn't
just mishear him?

00:22:12.650 --> 00:22:13.650
I didn't!

00:22:13.650 --> 00:22:16.070
You both did a good job!
Now get some rest!

00:22:16.110 --> 00:22:17.240
- Um, yes, sir!
- Yes, sir!

00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:19.200
Captain! It's the La Vie en Rose!

00:22:19.200 --> 00:22:20.160
What?

00:22:20.160 --> 00:22:21.370
It's approaching!

00:22:21.370 --> 00:22:23.160
They found us?

00:22:23.160 --> 00:22:24.370
Yes, sir!

00:22:45.850 --> 00:22:51.520
<i>michi mo nai areta genya ni
Amidst the wasteland without any roads...</i>

00:22:53.030 --> 00:22:58.740
<i>reeru wo tsukuru no wa kurushii koto sa
...it's difficult to lay down your rails.</i>

00:23:00.950 --> 00:23:03.240
<i>dakedo
However...</i>

00:23:03.240 --> 00:23:09.540
<i>tooi mukou mo shiranakucha ikenai
You've gotta know what's on the other side...</i>

00:23:09.540 --> 00:23:16.630
<i>boku-tachi wa kore kara nanda
...it's all from here on for us.</i>

00:23:16.630 --> 00:23:21.050
<i>"yume wo wasureta kodomo-tachi" to
"Children will forget their dreams"...</i>

00:23:21.050 --> 00:23:23.430
<i>hito wa iu
...is what they say.</i>

00:23:26.350 --> 00:23:33.650
<i>aa jidai ga naiteiru
Ah, the times are crying.</i>

00:23:47.230 --> 00:23:50.110
Since the La Vie en Rose
isn't any closer,

00:23:50.110 --> 00:23:53.400
Fa is getting more sentimental,
short-tempered, and hysterical.

00:23:53.440 --> 00:23:57.400
And it looks like there's someone aboard
the Argama who's helping Mashymre!

00:23:57.400 --> 00:23:58.700
Roux is smart, though,

00:23:58.700 --> 00:24:02.200
and brings us a new fighter
from the La Vie en Rose.

00:24:02.200 --> 00:24:04.870
You can't count on
dummy asteroids, after all!

00:24:05.120 --> 00:24:09.420
Next time, on Gundam ZZ:
"Sayonara, Fa."

00:24:09.830 --> 00:24:12.800
Poor Fa.

00:24:09.860 --> 00:24:12.950
SAYONARA, FA

00:24:09.860 --> 00:24:12.950
Next Time
